MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next addition because it would let my existing Echo devices control a lamp, adding a function I do not already have.",
    "The memory card and HDMI cable fit my history of adding storage and connecting equipment, although I would choose them only when a particular device or connection needs one."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Fire TV Sticks, Echo Dot and Echo Show repeat functions covered by my recent 4K Max, fourth-generation Dot and second-generation Show 5. Their similarity to things I own gives me little reason to choose them now.",
    "The tablets do not address a current need, and another portable speaker adds little when I already have an Amazon Tap and several Echo devices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My recent Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any Alexa device, even when it would duplicate something I just added.",
    "My history of buying electronics seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for more devices, while many of my purchases serve specific connection, replacement or accessory needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The generations of devices I recently added matter: an older version is not an appealing next purchase simply because it belongs to the same product family.",
    "My Echo Show stand and Harmony replacement batteries suggest that making equipment I already own more useful or keeping it working can matter more to me than adding another main device."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my connected-home and electronics interests but missed that I currently favor useful additions to my setup over older devices that repeat its functions."
}
